2025-06-12 04:03:46.036 | INFO     | llm_assistant:run:298 - ---responses in run: [{'prompt': [{'role': 'system', 'content': 'You are a senior software engineer who is best in the world at fixing vulnerabilities and patch porting between versions.\nUsers will give you 1. a patch based on a newer version 2. the diff info between the newer version and and older version. \nAnd you will generate a fix patch to the older version in the form of git diff based on the provided INSTRUCTION.\nINSTRUCTION:\nOnly reterun the final result after patch and diff information are entered. When all the information is entered, it will be identified with \u200d\u200d```===end===\u200d\u200d```\nOnly respond with the patch info, do not add any comments or change the indentation.\nThe patch should have no errors, it should compile and user should be able to use the fixed code as a direct replacement of the vulnerable code. The code should not introduce any new dependencies or use API calls that are not present in the code.\nIf you can generate a backport patch for the patch, do a brief change impact analysis to assess how these modifications might affect the overall system, considering both immediate and potential long-term compatibility issues.\nLow: Code diff will be applied to the code base and automatically merged without review.\nMedium: Code diff will be applied and a pull request will be sent to the developer to merge, but there are no indirect changes expected to be done in other parts of the system.\nHigh: Code diff will be offered as a suggestion to the developer to review and then apply to the code base. There are likely other changes that need to be done by the developer before the change can be implemented.\nPlease provide a response only in the following format:\n\nA. Commit message:\n<brief summary of the diff>\n\nB. Change summary:\n<description of the changes made in the diff>\n\nC. Compatibility Risk:\n<Low, Medium, High>\n\nD. Fixed Code:\n<original patch info with now backported>\n\n'}, {'role': 'system', 'content': "1. a patch based on a newer version: \nFrom 743eb6c68d3534e01e73d316ddcaa7334c0e29d3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001\nFrom: Pierre-Louis Bossart <pierre-louis.bossart@linux.intel.com>\nDate: Tue, 13 Feb 2024 12:12:41 +0200\nSubject: [PATCH] ASoC: SOF: topology: dynamically allocate and store DAI\n widget->private\nMIME-Version: 1.0\nContent-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8\nContent-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit\n\nFor dspless mode, we need to allocate and store an 'sdai'\nstructure. The existing code allocate the data on the stack and does\nnot set the widget->private pointer.\n\nThis minor change should not have any impact on existing DAIs, even\nwhen the DSP is used.\n\nSigned-off-by: Pierre-Louis Bossart <pierre-louis.bossart@linux.intel.com>\nReviewed-by: Péter Ujfalusi <peter.ujfalusi@linux.intel.com>\nReviewed-by: Bard Liao <yung-chuan.liao@linux.intel.com>\nSigned-off-by: Peter Ujfalusi <peter.ujfalusi@linux.intel.com>\nLink: https://msgid.link/r/20240213101247.28887-10-peter.ujfalusi@linux.intel.com\nSigned-off-by: Mark Brown <broonie@kernel.org>\n\ndiff --git a/sound/soc/sof/topology.c b/sound/soc/sof/topology.c\nindex 25fb0d1443b6..915c2e88e32b 100644\n--- a/sound/soc/sof/topology.c\n+++ b/sound/soc/sof/topology.c\n@@ -2356,23 +2356,29 @@ static int sof_dspless_widget_ready(struct snd_soc_component *scomp, int index,\n \tif (WIDGET_IS_DAI(w->id)) {\n \t\tstruct snd_sof_dev *sdev = snd_soc_component_get_drvdata(scomp);\n \t\tstruct snd_sof_widget *swidget;\n-\t\tstruct snd_sof_dai dai;\n+\t\tstruct snd_sof_dai *sdai;\n \t\tint ret;\n \n \t\tswidget = kzalloc(sizeof(*swidget), GFP_KERNEL);\n \t\tif (!swidget)\n \t\t\treturn -ENOMEM;\n \n-\t\tmemset(&dai, 0, sizeof(dai));\n+\t\tsdai = kzalloc(sizeof(*sdai), GFP_KERNEL);\n+\t\tif (!sdai) {\n+\t\t\tkfree(swidget);\n+\t\t\treturn -ENOMEM;\n+\t\t}\n \n-\t\tret = sof_connect_dai_widget(scomp, w, tw, &dai);\n+\t\tret = sof_connect_dai_widget(scomp, w, tw, sdai);\n \t\tif (ret) {\n \t\t\tkfree(swidget);\n+\t\t\tkfree(sdai);\n \t\t\treturn ret;\n \t\t}\n \n \t\tswidget->scomp = scomp;\n \t\tswidget->widget = w;\n+\t\tswidget->private = sdai;\n \t\tmutex_init(&swidget->setup_mutex);\n \t\tw->dobj.private = swidget;\n \t\tlist_add(&swidget->list, &sdev->widget_list);\n"}, {'role': 'system', 'content': '2. the diff info between the newer version and and older version: \n# 无法生成差异文件\n\n===end==='}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please return the final result.'}], 'response': 'A. Commit message:\nASoC: SOF: topology: dynamically allocate and store DAI widget->private\n\nB. Change summary:\nThe patch modifies the `sof_dspless_widget_ready` function to dynamically allocate memory for the `snd_sof_dai` structure (`sdai`) instead of using a stack-allocated variable. This change ensures that the `widget->private` pointer is properly set, which is necessary for the DSP-less mode. Additionally, error handling has been updated to free allocated memory if an error occurs during execution.\n\nC. Compatibility Risk:\nLow\n\nD. Fixed Code:\ndiff --git a/sound/soc/sof/topology.c b/sound/soc/sof/topology.c\nindex 25fb0d1443b6..915c2e88e32b 100644\n--- a/sound/soc/sof/topology.c\n+++ b/sound/soc/sof/topology.c\n@@ -2356,23 +2356,29 @@ static int sof_dspless_widget_ready(struct snd_soc_component *scomp, int index,\n \tif (WIDGET_IS_DAI(w->id)) {\n \t\tstruct snd_sof_dev *sdev = snd_soc_component_get_drvdata(scomp);\n \t\tstruct snd_sof_widget *swidget;\n-\t\tstruct snd_sof_dai dai;\n+\t\tstruct snd_sof_dai *sdai;\n \t\tint ret;\n \n \t\tswidget = kzalloc(sizeof(*swidget), GFP_KERNEL);\n \t\tif (!swidget)\n \t\t\treturn -ENOMEM;\n \n-\t\tmemset(&dai, 0, sizeof(dai));\n+\t\tsdai = kzalloc(sizeof(*sdai), GFP_KERNEL);\n+\t\tif (!sdai) {\n+\t\t\tkfree(swidget);\n+\t\t\treturn -ENOMEM;\n+\t\t}\n \n-\t\tret = sof_connect_dai_widget(scomp, w, tw, &dai);\n+\t\tret = sof_connect_dai_widget(scomp, w, tw, sdai);\n \t\tif (ret) {\n \t\t\tkfree(swidget);\n+\t\t\tkfree(sdai);\n \t\t\treturn ret;\n \t\t}\n \n \t\tswidget->scomp = scomp;\n \t\tswidget->widget = w;\n+\t\tswidget->private = sdai;\n \t\tmutex_init(&swidget->setup_mutex);\n \t\tw->dobj.private = swidget;\n \t\tlist_add(&swidget->list, &sdev->widget_list);', 'request_token': 0, 'response_token': 0}]
2025-06-12 04:03:46.037 | INFO     | modules.llm_adapter:_call_llm:973 - llm.run() result:{'openai_responses': ['A. Commit message:\nASoC: SOF: topology: dynamically allocate and store DAI widget->private\n\nB. Change summary:\nThe patch modifies the `sof_dspless_widget_ready` function to dynamically allocate memory for the `snd_sof_dai` structure (`sdai`) instead of using a stack-allocated variable. This change ensures that the `widget->private` pointer is properly set, which is necessary for the DSP-less mode. Additionally, error handling has been updated to free allocated memory if an error occurs during execution.\n\nC. Compatibility Risk:\nLow\n\nD. Fixed Code:\ndiff --git a/sound/soc/sof/topology.c b/sound/soc/sof/topology.c\nindex 25fb0d1443b6..915c2e88e32b 100644\n--- a/sound/soc/sof/topology.c\n+++ b/sound/soc/sof/topology.c\n@@ -2356,23 +2356,29 @@ static int sof_dspless_widget_ready(struct snd_soc_component *scomp, int index,\n \tif (WIDGET_IS_DAI(w->id)) {\n \t\tstruct snd_sof_dev *sdev = snd_soc_component_get_drvdata(scomp);\n \t\tstruct snd_sof_widget *swidget;\n-\t\tstruct snd_sof_dai dai;\n+\t\tstruct snd_sof_dai *sdai;\n \t\tint ret;\n \n \t\tswidget = kzalloc(sizeof(*swidget), GFP_KERNEL);\n \t\tif (!swidget)\n \t\t\treturn -ENOMEM;\n \n-\t\tmemset(&dai, 0, sizeof(dai));\n+\t\tsdai = kzalloc(sizeof(*sdai), GFP_KERNEL);\n+\t\tif (!sdai) {\n+\t\t\tkfree(swidget);\n+\t\t\treturn -ENOMEM;\n+\t\t}\n \n-\t\tret = sof_connect_dai_widget(scomp, w, tw, &dai);\n+\t\tret = sof_connect_dai_widget(scomp, w, tw, sdai);\n \t\tif (ret) {\n \t\t\tkfree(swidget);\n+\t\t\tkfree(sdai);\n \t\t\treturn ret;\n \t\t}\n \n \t\tswidget->scomp = scomp;\n \t\tswidget->widget = w;\n+\t\tswidget->private = sdai;\n \t\tmutex_init(&swidget->setup_mutex);\n \t\tw->dobj.private = swidget;\n \t\tlist_add(&swidget->list, &sdev->widget_list);'], 'request_tokens': [0], 'response_tokens': [0]}
